Well, I got the code up and running with all options.  The code itself
needs 644175 mem free to load, and after allocing for monsters, well all I'm
sure of is that it works with 689088 free.  To do this, I used my 386 to
backfill video memory from A000-B7FF, which works because the color graphics
adapter ram starts at b800.  I also had to change the /Gt:28 option to /Gt:1
so that all data got put into new segments, otherwise the stack and near
data got nickel and dimed into being > 64K.  If anyone out there can remap
to have 753664 bytes base ram, 689088 free, and CGA (or a disabled EGA) let
me know.
